    "description": "CheckSammy provides bulk waste, recycling, and sustainability services through a technology-enabled service network across North America. Its customers include multi-site commercial and industrial users that need recurring waste diversion, recycling, and sustainability program execution. The business follows an asset-light operating model built around software, service orchestration, and third-party service-provider networks rather than ownership of heavy disposal infrastructure. Public materials state that the company was founded in 2018 and serves more than 25,000 facilities across North America. I Squared led a $45 million strategic investment in January 2024 through its InfraTech strategy; the resulting ownership percentage is not publicly disclosed. The investment was positioned to support growth in waste diversion and sustainability workflow technology.",
